A||||5||Black88GT||Cavalier Z24 rim question||||1||
Z||000000||Black88GT||03-09-2001||09:57 PM||||While searching the forum, I have heard some conflicting statements regarding the offset of the 16" 5 star Z24 Cavalier rims from the later body style (not the brand new but the ones before that).  I was wondering who knows the offset for sure, and if they will protrude from the front wheel well on 88s like pre-88 GT wheels will. Also, any pics of these wheels on GT's would be appreciated, and any 88 owners that have installed them, their feedback would be appreciated.<P>TIA<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fieropage/af.bmp"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cooter||03-09-2001||10:11 PM||||I have the 16 inch Sunfire wheels on my 88 GT and I like the looks of them. The front wheels are a perfect offset, but the rear is sitting a little inside the wheelwell. If I can dig up the pictures, I will post them.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Black88GT||03-09-2001||10:38 PM||||Do you think if you added wider rear tires it would look a little better?  I can deal with that though, I was just worried about the front sticking out.  Great news!  You can fit 215/55 on the rear can't you? Then the fronts would be 205/55.  Is this right?<P>Thanks for the help!<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fieropage/af.bmp"> ||||reg||14
Z||000003||fierosound||03-09-2001||11:45 PM||||The Z24 5-spoke rims are only 6" wide with the same backspacing on the inside.  That's why they seem further in on the rear when compared to stock GT wheels which were 7" wide with the same backspacing.  It's not noticeable on the front - it looks OK.  I'm running 205/55/16 front, and 215/55/16 rear.  I wouldn't want to mount a wider tire on a 6" rim...||||reg||10
Z||000004||Black88GT||03-09-2001||11:55 PM||||Is it that noticeable on the rear?  Is your name Tony by any chance, because the only picture I have of the wheels on a GT is a maroon GT like yours and its labeled "tonys87.jpg"<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fieropage/af.bmp"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||fierosound||03-10-2001||12:22 AM||||That's the one.  You'll notice that the splash shield is quite visible in the rear wheelwell.  But that's at a low angle in the picture and I don't think anyone else would really notice - just me.  I was thinking I'd get longer wheel studs and put a 3/8 or 1/2 spacer behind the wheel.  BUT that's something I really don't want to do.  I'd look pretty silly snapping a wheel off at a race!!||||reg||1
